---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import StoryTimeline from '../components/StoryTimeline.astro';
import poster199x from '../assets/brand/hornero-199x-poster.jpg';
import { story } from '../data/story';
import { pins, releases, themes, short } from '../data/product';

const shell = pins.shell;
const config = pins.config;
const hornero = pins.hornero;
const currentRelease = releases.find((release) => release.status === 'tagged');
---

<SiteLayout
  socialImage="/og/roots.png"
  socialImageAlt="The HorneroOS timeline from 2018 to 2026, with the 2018 stage dashed because it rests on the maintainer's account."
  title="Roots — Hornero OS"
  description="How Hornero grew from a personal desktop configuration into an open operating-system project, with its sources and credits intact."
>
  <section class="intro section">
    <p class="plate-id"><strong>Archivo 2018 — hoy</strong><span>ARG / 199X</span><span>Las raíces del proyecto</span></p>
    <h1>
      Built from a desktop.
      <br />
      <em>Grown into a system.</em>
    </h1>
    <p>
      Hornero began as a personal configuration, then grew into a set of maintained projects for the shell, themes,
      operating-system tools, testing and documentation.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section timeline-section" id="timeline" aria-labelledby="timeline-title">
    <div class="timeline-head">
      <h2 id="timeline-title">From a workstation to an operating system.</h2>
      <p>
        Two histories run through this page: a personal desktop that has been in daily use since 2018, and a set of
        standalone HorneroOS projects that began in September 2026. A dashed rule marks the stage git cannot confirm;
        every other row links to the commit or tag that dates it. The current Quickshell shell is not the 2018 setup
        unchanged.
      </p>
    </div>
    <StoryTimeline entries={story} variant="ledger" label="HorneroOS timeline, 2018 to 2026" />
  </section>

  <section class="section identity" aria-labelledby="identity-title">
    <figure class="poster">
      <img
        src={poster199x.src}
        width={poster199x.width}
        height={poster199x.height}
        loading="lazy"
        decoding="async"
        alt="Illustration of a hornero bird and its arched mud nest over a midnight-blue street grid cut by a diagonal avenue, under a signal-orange sun. It is artwork, not a desktop screenshot."
      />
      <figcaption>Hornero 199X artwork · AI-assisted illustration, directed and reviewed by the project · not a screenshot</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <div class="identity-copy">
      <h2 id="identity-title">Where the look comes from.</h2>
      <p>
        Hornero 199X borrows from Argentine broadcast graphics, home-computer magazines and arcades, from La Plata’s
        street grid cut by diagonals, and from the hornero’s clay nest. It is an artistic direction, not a historical
        product. The photographs behind the Hornero Originals themes are licensed and credited on the{' '}
        <a href="/wallpapers">wallpapers page</a>.
      </p>
      <p><a href="/docs/development/design-language/">Read the design language</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section map-section" id="repositories" aria-labelledby="repositories-title">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Maintained in clear pieces</p>
      <h2 id="repositories-title">Core repositories, clear boundaries.</h2>
      <p>
        The product components are maintained separately so each layer can be reviewed, packaged and tested at the right
        boundary. The{' '}
        <a href="https://github.com/HorneroOS/.github/blob/main/governance/docs/repository-map.md">
          full organization map
        </a>{' '}
        also covers Docs, Website, QA and shared governance.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="repo-list">
      <a href={`${shell.repo}/tree/${shell.sha}`}>
        <span class="repo-mark">01</span>
        <span>
          <strong>Shell</strong>
          <small>Quickshell runtime, layout presets, Companion and shell services</small>
        </span>
        <code>{short(shell.sha)}</code>
      </a>
      <a href={`${config.repo}/tree/${config.sha}`}>
        <span class="repo-mark">02</span>
        <span>
          <strong>Config</strong>
          <small>Appearance packs, defaults, brand assets and package data</small>
        </span>
        <code>{short(config.sha)}</code>
      </a>
      <a href={`${hornero.repo}/tree/${hornero.sha}`}>
        <span class="repo-mark">03</span>
        <span>
          <strong>Hornero</strong>
          <small>Native CLI, release compositions and system capabilities</small>
        </span>
        <code>{short(hornero.sha)}</code>
      </a>
      <a href="https://github.com/HorneroOS/greeter">
        <span class="repo-mark">04</span>
        <span>
          <strong>Greeter</strong>
          <small>Hornero’s SDDM login screen and its Qt 6 runtime</small>
        </span>
        <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
      </a>
      <a href="https://github.com/HorneroOS/installer">
        <span class="repo-mark">05</span>
        <span>
          <strong>Installer</strong>
          <small>Staged installation contract; a public ISO is not available yet</small>
        </span>
        <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
      </a>
      <a href="https://github.com/HorneroOS/qa">
        <span class="repo-mark">06</span>
        <span>
          <strong>QA</strong>
          <small>Virtual-machine journeys and evidence for complete product builds</small>
        </span>
        <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section contributor-guide" id="contribute" aria-labelledby="contributor-guide-title">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">For contributors</p>
      <h2 id="contributor-guide-title">Start with the shared design language.</h2>
      <p>
        It sets cross-project identity and interaction principles. Each repository remains the source for its own
        implementation rules and tested capabilities.
      </p>
    </div>
    <nav aria-label="Contributor references">
      <a href="/docs/development/design-language/">
        <span>Product policy</span>
        <strong>
          HorneroOS design language <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
        </strong>
      </a>
      <a href="https://github.com/HorneroOS/.github/blob/main/governance/docs/repository-map.md">
        <span>Ownership</span>
        <strong>
          Repository map <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
        </strong>
      </a>
      <a href="https://github.com/HorneroOS/.github/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md">
        <span>Workflow</span>
        <strong>
          Contribution guide <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
        </strong>
      </a>
    </nav>
  </section>

  <section class="section lineage" id="community">
    <p class="eyebrow">Influence, credit and direction</p>
    <h2>Learn from good work. Keep our own shape.</h2>
    <div class="lineage-grid">
      <article>
        <h3>Code ancestry</h3>
        <p>
          The Quickshell shell is adapted from <a href="https://github.com/caelestia-dots/shell">Caelestia Shell</a>.
          The upstream author, license and imported commit remain documented in the repository.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <h3>Design references</h3>
        <p>
          <a href="https://github.com/Ryoku-dev/ryoku">Ryoku</a>,{' '}
          <a href="https://github.com/AvengeMedia/DankMaterialShell">DankMaterialShell</a> and{' '}
          <a href="https://github.com/omacom/omarchy">Omarchy</a> help us study how other teams make settings
          discoverable, themes coherent and Linux desktops approachable.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <h3>Hornero’s direction</h3>
        <p>
          Those references inform the questions we ask, not the answers we copy. Hornero keeps its own visual range,
          open development and product decisions.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <h3>People behind HorneroOS</h3>
        <p>
          <a href="https://github.com/ulises-jeremias">Ulises Jeremías</a> is HorneroOS’s principal maintainer.{' '}
          <a href="https://github.com/PandaFoss">Panda Foss</a> contributes to HorneroOS and is one of the maintainers
          of <a href="https://gitlab.com/anarchyinstaller/installer">Anarchy Linux</a>. Panda will lead development of
          HorneroOS’s future custom installer. The current <a href="/install">Calamares path</a> remains provisional
          until that installer is ready. Both are part of the{' '}
          <a href="https://github.com/HorneroOS">HorneroOS organization</a>.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
    <p class="source-line">
      Sources checked at Shell{' '}
      <a href={`${shell.repo}/commit/${shell.sha}`}>
        <code>{short(shell.sha)}</code>
      </a>
      , Config{' '}
      <a href={`${config.repo}/commit/${config.sha}`}>
        <code>{short(config.sha)}</code>
      </a>{' '}
      and Hornero{' '}
      <a href={`${hornero.repo}/commit/${hornero.sha}`}>
        <code>{short(hornero.sha)}</code>
      </a>
      . The pinned sources define {themes.length} theme packs
      {currentRelease && (
        <>
          {' '}
          and include the tagged composition <a href={`/releases#${currentRelease.name}`}>{currentRelease.name}</a>
        </>
      )}
      .
    </p>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>

<style>
  .intro {
    padding-block: clamp(1rem, 4vw, 4rem) 1.5rem;
  }
  .intro h1 {
    margin-top: 0.7rem;
    font-size: clamp(3rem, 2rem + 5vw, 6.2rem);
    line-height: 0.98;
    letter-spacing: -0.055em;
  }
  .intro h1 em {
    color: var(--accent);
    font-style: normal;
  }
  .intro > p:last-child {
    max-width: 59ch;
    margin-top: 1.2rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-size: var(--step-1);
  }
  .timeline-section > h2,
  .map-section h2,
  .contributor-guide h2,
  .lineage > h2 {
    margin-top: 0.4rem;
  }
  .repo-mark {
    color: var(--secondary);
    font: 0.75rem var(--font-data);
  }
  .map-section {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1.5rem;
    padding: clamp(1.3rem, 4vw, 2.6rem);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    background: var(--surface);
  }
  .map-section > div:first-child > p:last-child {
    margin-top: 0.55rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }
  .repo-list {
    display: grid;
  }
  .repo-list > a {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 2rem 1fr auto;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.6rem;
    min-width: 0;
    padding: 0.9rem 0.1rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
    color: var(--text);
    text-decoration: none;
  }
  .repo-list strong,
  .repo-list small {
    display: block;
  }
  .repo-list small {
    margin-top: 0.12rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }
  .repo-list code {
    color: var(--secondary);
  }
  .repo-list a:hover strong {
    color: var(--accent);
  }
  .contributor-guide {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1.5rem;
    padding-inline-start: clamp(1rem, 3vw, 2rem);
    border-inline-start: 2px solid var(--highlight);
  }
  .contributor-guide > div > p:last-child {
    max-width: 58ch;
    margin-top: 0.55rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }
  .contributor-guide nav {
    display: grid;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  .contributor-guide nav a {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.25rem;
    padding: 0.8rem 0.1rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
    text-decoration: none;
  }
  .contributor-guide nav a > span {
    color: var(--secondary);
    font: 0.68rem var(--font-data);
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }
  .contributor-guide nav a strong {
    color: var(--text);
  }
  .contributor-guide nav a:hover strong {
    color: var(--accent);
  }
  .lineage-grid {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.8rem;
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
  }
  .lineage-grid article {
    padding: 1rem 1.1rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    background: var(--surface);
  }
  .lineage-grid p {
    margin-top: 0.35rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }
  .source-line {
    margin-top: 1.4rem;
    padding-top: 1rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-size: 0.82rem;
  }
  @media (min-width: 900px) {
    .map-section {
      grid-template-columns: 0.7fr 1.3fr;
      align-items: start;
    }
    .contributor-guide {
      grid-template-columns: 0.7fr 1.3fr;
      align-items: start;
    }
    .lineage-grid {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    }
  }
  .timeline-head { display: grid; gap: 1rem clamp(1.5rem, 5vw, 5rem); margin-bottom: 1.5rem; }
  .timeline-head h2 { font-size: clamp(1.9rem, 1.2rem + 2.8vw, 3.4rem); line-height: 1.02; letter-spacing: -0.04em; }
  .timeline-head p { max-width: 58ch; color: var(--text-muted); }
  .identity { display: grid; gap: clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 4rem); align-items: center; }
  .poster { margin: 0; border: 1px solid var(--line); background: var(--surface); }
  .poster img { width: 100%; height: auto; }
  .poster figcaption { padding: 0.6rem 0.8rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); color: var(--text-muted); font: 0.68rem var(--font-data); font-stretch: 87.5%; }
  .identity-copy { display: grid; gap: 1rem; }
  .identity-copy h2 { font-size: clamp(1.7rem, 1.2rem + 2vw, 2.8rem); line-height: 1.05; letter-spacing: -0.04em; }
  .identity-copy p { max-width: 50ch; color: var(--text-muted); }
  @media (min-width: 900px) {
    .timeline-head { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 6fr) minmax(0, 5fr); align-items: end; }
    .identity { grid-template-columns: 1.1fr 0.9fr; }
  }
</style>

<style>
  /* 199X per-page direction: roots as an archival timeline. */
  .repo-mark { font-family: var(--font-data); }
  .lineage-grid > * { border-radius: 2px; }
</style>
